      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Senator Halloway calms the rising tension by stating that total data access is a pragmatic necessity to prevent future catastrophes from the Anarchist Free Council. The young activist, Elena, passionately shoves the file away at her rationality, screaming that \"security isn't the right name for the right to blanket kill us.\" As the room grows cold with unspoken threats, she finally collapses into a sob while the senator simply watches the silence settle over them.\n\nI suggest you end the scene with the senator already signing the decree, leaving the activist alone in the next shadow to make the power imbalance even more palpable.",
